  <event id="232">
      <start>14:00</start>
      <duration>00:45</duration>
      <room>AW1.120</room>
      <slug></slug>
      <title>MDB and MDBX: Open Source SimpleDB Projects based on GTM</title>
      <subtitle></subtitle>
      <track>NoSQL</track>
      <type></type>
      <language></language>
      <abstract>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;M/DB is an Open Source emulation of Amazon SimpleDB, whilst M/DBX is an Open Source Native XML Database based around the SimpleDB HTTP-based API model. Both projects have been built on top of the GT.M NoSQL database.&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;  </abstract>
      <description>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;This talk will briefly summarise the capabilities of these two databases and typical use-cases for which they are designed.  It will also examine why GT.M was chosen as the underlying NoSQL database technology on which they were built.&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;  </description>
      <persons>
          <person id="2321">Rob Tweed</person>
      </persons>
      <links></links>
      <video></video>
      <end></end>
  </event>